<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 0.96 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 0.96 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.2885 to the dollar, up from 3.2890 on Tuesday and at 1.8785 to the mark, up from 1.8850, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.96 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Tuesday's 0.73 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
